  "question": {
    "text": "<p>A swimmer wants to cross a river from point <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math>&nbsp;to point <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi></math>. Line AB makes an angle of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>30</mn><mo>&#176;</mo></math> with the flow of the river. The magnitude&nbsp;of the velocity of the swimmer is the same as that of the river. The angle <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#952;</mi></math> with the line <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi></math> should be _______<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#176;</mo></math>, so that the swimmer reaches point <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi></math>.</p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/98366fc6-e95e-40f5-9298-e8ea474198df-image.png\" style=\"width: 252px; height: 218px;\" /></p>",
